    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so they're basically just a middleman to make sure nobody gets scammed, right? what happens if something goes wrong during the inspections and we decide not to move forward? does the escrow person just give the money back to me?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Exactly, you can think of the escrow agent as the highly organized, rule-following middleman. If you and the seller agree that the deal is falling apart—perhaps because the inspection revealed a major issue—the escrow agent facilitates the termination of the contract. They are responsible for following the terms of the agreement, which usually dictates how and when any deposits, like your earnest money, are returned to you. They act as the gatekeeper, ensuring the money moves according to the agreed-upon rules, not based on a sudden whim.",
